Licences, as found in the files
-------------------------------
- libgcc2.c: GPL version 2 or later, PLUS the libgcc special exception ("if you
  link this library with other files, some of which are compiled with GCC, to
  produce an executable, this library does not by itself cause the resulting
  executable to be covered by the GNU General Public License").
- longlong.h: GPL version 2 or later. At this revision its header carries NO
  exception text of its own. libgcc2.c includes it, so it is compiled into
  every libgcc2 member. What that means for the linking exception is recorded
  as an open question for the project owner, not decided here.
- COPYING: the GNU General Public License, version 2, from the same revision.

Project-written files (NOT GCC source)
--------------------------------------
- shim/tconfig.h, shim/machmode.h, shim/defaults.h, shim/stddef.h: stand-ins
  for the headers libgcc2.c reads from a GCC build tree, which does not exist
  here. Each says so in its first line. They carry target facts only
  (mips/R5900, little-endian, 32-bit size_t).
- MEMBERS: which archive members are built, from which file, with GCC's own
  module selection (-DFINE_GRAINED_LIBRARIES -DL_<module>).
- LINK_ALIASES: names a member references that the game defines under its
  splat name (link-only; the file says why they are not symbol_addrs rows).
- PROVENANCE: this file.

How it is built and linked
--------------------------
tools/ee/build_libgcc.sh <region> (called by tools/ee/build.sh) builds each
member the region's linker script names — a splat `lib` subsegment,
`libgcc.a:<member>.o` in going-decompiled/config/<region>/*.yaml — with the
SDK's own compiler, 2.9-ee-991111 cpp.exe + cc1.exe at -O2 -G0, and archives
them into going-decompiled/build/<region>/lib/libgcc.a. The ee-gcc driver
segfaults under wibo, so its predefines are passed by hand; the cc1 output goes
through tools/ee/move_fixup.sed like every unit's (an assembler-input rewrite,
not a source edit).

Members linked today (USA): _divdi3 (__divdi3 at 0x11FC68, __clz_tab at
0x13AC58), _fixunsdfdi (__fixunsdfdi at 0x1212C8), _floatdidf (__floatdidf at
0x1213B8) and _muldi3 (__muldi3 at 0x121AB8). _fixunsdfdi and _floatdidf need
the li.d -> dli rewrite of cc1's output (tools/ee/libgcc_lid_dli.pl) and, for
_fixunsdfdi's call to dptoul, the link-only alias in LINK_ALIASES. Each was checked against the
SDK's own libgcc.a member (tools/ee/cc/lib/gcc-lib/ee/2.95.2/libgcc.a, used
only as an identity oracle, never linked): .text, .rodata and .data bytes and
the relocation lists are identical. The whole-image check is landing_gate.sh.
